WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:03.360
Let's talk a little bit about the lesser characters of Bloodborne.

00:00:03.549 --> 00:00:10.169
Their stories aren't quite as powerful as some of the characters that I've covered in Prepare To Cry, but there are so many fascinating

00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:17.729
details within their quest lines, most of which you probably didn't even come across because these stories are really quite hidden.

00:00:18.070 --> 00:00:20.639
Here are 10 of them, let me know if you've found them.

00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:27.449
This is the Narrow-Minded man who goes to Oedon Chapel if you tell him to go to Iosefka's Clinic.

00:00:27.490 --> 00:00:30.809
He does the exact opposite of everything you tell him to do,

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:37.500
but I think he's interesting because I'm confident that the exact opposite of everything he says is true.

00:00:37.870 --> 00:00:39.870
"I'll spare you one nugget of advice:

00:00:40.660 --> 00:00:42.660
Beware the lady of the night.

00:00:43.360 --> 00:00:47.189
I can see in her eyes, she deeply resents the young saint.

00:00:48.520 --> 00:00:53.219
She hears people whisper. She knows what people think of her. Yes...

00:00:54.940 --> 00:00:58.320
She despises the saint for having what she doesn't."

00:00:59.079 --> 00:01:01.079
Truth is, it's the other way around:

00:01:01.660 --> 00:01:07.290
Adella, the 'Blood Saint' that you saved from Yahar-Gul appears to despise Arianna the whore.

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:13.739
Whenever you talk to Arianna, you can actually see Adella and eavesdropping on you from the other side of the Chapel.

00:01:13.810 --> 00:01:17.280
It's quite creepy, actually. Look at her.

00:01:17.280 --> 00:01:19.320
Anyway, these characters have something in common and

00:01:19.990 --> 00:01:27.809
it's that they both offer you their blood in some sort of gratitude for saving them. If you accept Arianna's blood, it reads:

00:01:28.030 --> 00:01:34.589
"A member of the Old Healing Church would know that her blood is similar indeed to precisely what was once forbidden."

00:01:36.079 --> 00:01:42.009
Adella watches you accepting Arianna's blood; the jealousy building up inside of her. Imagine:

00:01:42.140 --> 00:01:46.149
she's watching her savior accept forbidden blood over her own.

00:01:46.490 --> 00:01:53.229
She has this gratitude to you for saving her, but what you're doing is a great sin in her eyes and

00:01:53.869 --> 00:02:00.999
eventually it becomes too much. If you take Arianna's blood more than three times before the Blood Moon, then you explode.

00:02:01.939 --> 00:02:07.449
Just kidding. Why did I explode there? I don't know the lore on that one. Anyway, I assume it's a glitch,

00:02:07.940 --> 00:02:09.319
but if you do accept

00:02:09.319 --> 00:02:16.449
Arianna's blood more than three times before the Blood Moon, then Arianna lies dead and the blood is on Adella's hands.

00:02:16.790 --> 00:02:19.840
Literally, "I only wished to be of help.

00:02:21.530 --> 00:02:23.530
Take my blood [Wincing SFX]"

00:02:24.620 --> 00:02:28.269
It got me thinking. What could be so wrong with Arianna's blood?

00:02:28.310 --> 00:02:34.690
What could be so forbidden about it? And now, after working on my last video which was about Cainhurst,

00:02:35.030 --> 00:02:37.030
it becomes pretty clear:

00:02:37.190 --> 00:02:44.810
Arianna wears a noble dress, right? And this is a dress that's worn by the nobles of the old bloodline that traces back to Cainhurst.

00:02:44.810 --> 00:02:47.049
Cainhurst is the home to the Vilebloods.

00:02:47.299 --> 00:02:53.229
The vampire like humans that rival the Healing Church of Yharnam, and as Alfred tells us, the Cainhurst

00:02:53.660 --> 00:02:57.789
Vilebloods are born of forbidden blood that was stolen from Yharnam.

00:02:58.420 --> 00:03:04.380
So somehow, Arianna is descended from the Vilebloods and Adella knows it.

00:03:05.480 --> 00:03:07.520
[Crazed giggles]

00:03:08.040 --> 00:03:10.420
" [More Crazed Giggles] My sweet Hunter

00:03:12.860 --> 00:03:20.120
Your blood is tainted. I can-... I can't help myself [Even More Crazed Giggles]"

00:03:25.220 --> 00:03:27.079
This is the Chapel Dweller.

00:03:27.079 --> 00:03:34.719
He's one of the kindest characters in Bloodborne. You invite everybody to this sanctuary because he asked you to and

00:03:35.000 --> 00:03:41.229
he gets an immense sense of pride knowing that he is in some way responsible for the people's lives here.

00:03:41.630 --> 00:03:43.959
"I've never been any use to anyone you see.

00:03:44.780 --> 00:03:47.380
Just happy about it is all. [Wheezed Laughter]"

00:03:48.739 --> 00:03:56.649
But then you are playing Bloodborne, after all, so all the characters in the chapel begin to die, one by one. "Was it a Beast?

00:03:57.979 --> 00:04:04.119
Or could someone from outside have come in and I- I just don't know.[Weeping Sounds]"

00:04:09.019 --> 00:04:14.198
"Blimey! Don't scare me like that on a night like this, I took you for a monster.

00:04:15.560 --> 00:04:19.449
Oh, thank the stars, you're fairly normal. Well, if you're a hunter,

00:04:20.300 --> 00:04:23.739
then would you know of any safe Havens?"

00:04:24.350 --> 00:04:30.279
First to die: the Narrow-Minded Man, then the Old Woman, then Adella, then the Dweller, and

00:04:30.830 --> 00:04:32.509
finally, Arianna.

00:04:32.509 --> 00:04:36.939
Confront the Beggar at any point during all of this and he transforms.

00:04:38.420 --> 00:04:43.440
"Have you got a screw loose, or is it your animal intuition?

00:04:44.240 --> 00:04:46.900
You hunters have got more blood on your hands.

00:04:49.600 --> 00:04:51.940
You are a sick puppy."

00:04:52.760 --> 00:04:56.000
"You drink the blood of half the town and now this!

00:04:56.360 --> 00:05:00.969
And you talk of Beasts?! You hunters are the real killers!"

00:05:01.970 --> 00:05:08.680
It's better to send this guy to Iosefka's Clinic instead where he meets a bit more of a celestial fate.

00:05:08.900 --> 00:05:15.460
In fact, Iosefka's Clinic, by this point in the game, isn't actually run by the real Iosefka anymore.

00:05:15.590 --> 00:05:18.129
A keen player might have noticed what changes.

00:05:18.200 --> 00:05:21.370
"Are you out on the hunt?

00:05:22.130 --> 00:05:24.340
Then I'm very sorry, but I

00:05:25.100 --> 00:05:27.100
cannot open this door.

00:05:27.680 --> 00:05:29.180
I am Iosefka.

00:05:30.160 --> 00:05:33.400
The patients here in my clinic must not be exposed to infection.

00:05:34.300 --> 00:05:38.280
I know that you hunt for us, for our town, but I'm sorry.

00:05:39.260 --> 00:05:41.260
I pray for your safety."

00:05:42.650 --> 00:05:44.650
"Oh! Well, hello!

00:05:46.400 --> 00:05:53.169
Splendid! Let me ask you a small kindness: you're soon off to hunt I presume?

00:05:54.580 --> 00:05:57.520
Then, if you find any survivors,

00:05:58.800 --> 00:06:00.680
tell them to seek Iosefka's Clinic.

00:06:01.970 --> 00:06:09.519
Upon my hippocratic oath, if they are yet human, I will look after them; perhaps even cure them.

00:06:11.060 --> 00:06:15.800
This sickness, these beasts; they are not to be feared.

00:06:17.180 --> 00:06:23.220
This time the night is long. I may be trapped here, but I should do something to help.

00:06:25.720 --> 00:06:28.720
I'll even offer a reward for your cooperation.

00:06:30.500 --> 00:06:31.220
Tempted?"

00:06:32.180 --> 00:06:38.760
The real Iosefka is this kind-hearted woman who treats a few patients at her clinic and absolutely

00:06:39.110 --> 00:06:43.990
refuses to open the door, for it would put her patients at risk of catching the scourge.

00:06:44.270 --> 00:06:51.879
Note how she doesn't want anyone else to enter her clinic, but this all changes once you enter Cathedral Ward and

00:06:52.460 --> 00:06:55.699
we never hear from the real Iosefka again.

00:06:56.760 --> 00:07:01.639
If you enter the clinic from behind, you discover what became of the original Iosefka and,

00:07:02.160 --> 00:07:05.479
indeed, all the patients of the clinic if you sent them here.

00:07:05.660 --> 00:07:10.680
The Imposter, who is up stairs and garbed in the White of the Choir, has been experimenting

00:07:10.760 --> 00:07:15.740
on all the humans you brought here, somehow transforming them into these Celestial Beings.

00:07:16.590 --> 00:07:19.459
Gascoigne's daughter, Adella, Arianna; all

00:07:20.040 --> 00:07:25.099
mutated by this woman who wants to rise above humanity's beastly stupidity.

00:07:26.010 --> 00:07:31.010
If you confront her before the Blood Moon has risen, then you to engage in fighting.

00:07:31.139 --> 00:07:36.139
But if you confront her when the blood moon is in the sky then, "God, I'm nauseous

00:07:37.979 --> 00:07:39.979
Have you found this?

00:07:41.040 --> 00:07:44.719
It's progressing. I can see things.

00:07:46.320 --> 00:07:51.800
I knew it...I'm different. I'm no beast. I'm-

00:07:53.680 --> 00:07:56.600
Oh God, it feels awful, but...

00:07:58.020 --> 00:08:00.020
...it proves that I'm chosen...

00:08:01.860 --> 00:08:10.100
Don't you see? How they rive, rive inside, my head? It's rather

00:08:11.160 --> 00:08:16.260
rapturous then. [Crazed Giggles]"

00:08:16.620 --> 00:08:20.920
Moving on to a couple of other characters that we found in the early stages of Yharnam:

00:08:20.940 --> 00:08:25.249
did any of you guys actually follow through with the lonely old woman's quest line?

00:08:25.470 --> 00:08:29.839
She will continue to curse and blame you for everything bad that's happening in Yharnam.

00:08:29.840 --> 00:08:33.900
But as time goes on, and as you kill more bosses, she starts

00:08:33.960 --> 00:08:39.660
self-medicating herself with sedatives to ward off the despair and she becomes quite delusional.

00:08:40.460 --> 00:08:45.400
"Oh now now, have some patience; that will make everything better."

00:08:46.710 --> 00:08:52.549
If you keep talking to her then she passes these sedatives on to you and after accepting three times

00:08:52.560 --> 00:08:58.970
she'll run out and go outside to look for more sedatives. It's at this point that you can talk to the Chapel Dweller and

00:08:59.520 --> 00:09:02.620
discover her fate. "The Old girl you sent over?

00:09:02.760 --> 00:09:04.590
She's dead.

00:09:04.590 --> 00:09:09.079
Killed, stomped dead." She's been murdered outside next to one of the graves.

00:09:10.440 --> 00:09:14.570
Moving on, another NPC who meets a really cruel fate is Gilbert,

00:09:14.700 --> 00:09:21.140
who you probably forgot about. He was the guy at the start in central Yharnam who offers you advice as you go through the game.

00:09:21.390 --> 00:09:28.910
He mentions that he's lucky not to be afflicted by the plague of beasts and that imbibing the old blood granted him time.

00:09:29.490 --> 00:09:37.070
Unfortunately for him, like many others in Yharnam, his legs are failing him and he waits out the night of the hunt indoors,

00:09:37.410 --> 00:09:39.410
offering some advice to passers-by.

00:09:39.720 --> 00:09:43.999
After killing Gascoigne, he gives you the flamesprayer, which a couple of you might have missed,

00:09:44.070 --> 00:09:48.410
but did you also know that he turns into a beast after the Blood Moon rises?

00:09:48.810 --> 00:09:51.530
Apparently, he wasn't as safe as he thought he was.

00:09:52.290 --> 00:09:57.320
After you've killed Vicar Amelia, these lit windows become occupied by Patches the Spider.

00:09:57.840 --> 00:10:02.989
Patches returns once again with sinister motives just like before. He offers you up for

00:10:03.090 --> 00:10:10.819
sacrifice to his God and then kicks you off a ledge; all standard stuff. And as usual, when you confront, him he begs your forgiveness.

00:10:11.430 --> 00:10:14.090
Now, in previous games, after this,

00:10:14.580 --> 00:10:19.999
after you forgive him for kicking you down a ledge, he usually becomes a merchant. And in Bloodborne,

00:10:20.000 --> 00:10:23.270
you're probably thinking that he doesn't become a merchant.

00:10:23.270 --> 00:10:28.759
Well, he does. He's just incredibly difficult to find. So, he appears in the Chalice Dungeons,

00:10:28.760 --> 00:10:32.869
but he's so difficult to find, that I looked for him for like a solid day

00:10:32.870 --> 00:10:39.950
and I still couldn't find him, so let me know if you do. In the Chalice Dungeons, he sells everything that the Bath Messengers sell,

00:10:40.140 --> 00:10:43.819
but at a really high price, which makes absolutely no sense

00:10:44.310 --> 00:10:50.000
for how difficult he is to find, so there's really no reason to search him out in the Chalice Dungeons,

00:10:50.130 --> 00:10:53.780
unless you really really need some Blood Vials or something.

00:10:54.590 --> 00:10:59.410
Anyway, also in the Chalice Dungeons is an item called the Ring of Betrothal.

00:10:59.930 --> 00:11:06.639
The ring was once used in the age of the Great Ones and it was used in a time where marriage was a Blood Contract.

00:11:07.460 --> 00:11:11.650
Because the ring was given to those who were chosen to bear a special child.

00:11:11.890 --> 00:11:18.790
So, assumedly, Queen Yharnam was once the holder of this ring because she was a woman who bore the child of a Great One. and

00:11:19.160 --> 00:11:23.110
And you can even take this ring to Queen Annalise who's the ruler of the Vilebloods.

00:11:23.690 --> 00:11:27.249
You can even propose to your queen, even though she shuts you down.

00:11:28.400 --> 00:11:30.400
"Speak not those words.

00:11:31.370 --> 00:11:33.519
We have little need of a consort.

00:11:35.060 --> 00:11:38.499
Such a path would be likely to lead to further ruin

00:11:40.370 --> 00:11:42.399
Thou art Dear to us.

00:11:44.300 --> 00:11:47.529
We would see no harm befall thee."

00:11:48.710 --> 00:11:54.129
And that's it. Those are 10 character quest lines that are slightly hard to follow. The thing is though,

00:11:54.130 --> 00:11:58.930
I didn't really want this video to be super long, so I didn't include all of their dialogue.

00:11:59.300 --> 00:12:01.990
But in the description are links to two places:

00:12:02.420 --> 00:12:09.069
one is to a channel called MoonlightButterfly, where you can find all the dialogue in Bloodborne recorded and

00:12:09.590 --> 00:12:14.649
categorized and uploaded for you to enjoy. The other location is simply the FextraLife Wiki

00:12:14.780 --> 00:12:18.370
so you can learn about how to follow these quest lines for yourself.

00:12:18.370 --> 00:12:24.370
I recommend you check out both of these places if you want to learn more and thanks for watching guys. As a side note,

00:12:24.370 --> 00:12:27.579
I'm kind of thinking of moving away from Bloodborne in the next few videos.

00:12:27.580 --> 00:12:29.920
I ran this poll on Twitter

00:12:29.920 --> 00:12:35.499
and it showed me that not as many followers as I thought actually owned Bloodborne.

00:12:35.500 --> 00:12:38.860
So, maybe we'll move back to Dark Souls 1 &amp; 2 and

00:12:38.990 --> 00:12:44.799
some Demon Souls and branch out a little bit more so, thanks for watching guys anyway, and I'll see you in the next one.

